    "capturedOn": "2026-09-30",
    "productVersion": "manufacturing.zeenea.app/studio",
    "screenshot": "captures/asset-detail-360.png"
  },
  "reference": "product",
  "slots": {
    "header": "Breadcrumb, then the identity row (item type tag, Shared tag, title, lifecycle stage tag, Actions button) over three metadata lines: technical name, a catalog / data product / connection path with links, and a last-updated date.",
    "tabs": "The item's facets (eight on a Dataset), some carrying a count, one greyed when the source supplies nothing. Opposite them, two avatar stacks: curators and contacts, which are a summary of the People panel.",
    "left": "Authored narrative: access-request policy select, glossary multi-select of removable chips, a description block (use-source checkbox, summary, full rich-text description), and a relations section that is empty far more often than not.",
    "right": "Completion meter, then a second tab set. Properties is a long form in the item type's groups (DATA Contract, OUTPUT PORT, Cataloging, GOVERNANCE) mixing selects, multi-selects, text and date fields, ending in a read-only source-properties list.",
    "right-people": "Not drawn here. Two role sections (Curator, Contact), each with an add-person icon action and a two-column grid of avatar, name and a remove control.",
    "right-suggestions": "Not drawn here. A four-way segmented control (Accepted, Rejected, Pending, All) over suggestion cards: author avatar, name, relative time, status at the right, body text, a comment textarea, and a Reject/Accept footer pair.",
    "toast": "Not drawn here. A transient error toast appears bottom-centre on a slow response. It is real chrome on this page, and the DS tier has no toast component to carry it."
  },
  "undrawnSlots": [
    "right-people",
    "right-suggestions",
    "toast"
  ],
  "renderNotes": [
    "Inside a VERTICAL frame, never set `sizing.horizontal:\"FILL\"`. `render-node.js` emits `flex:1` for it with no axis awareness, so in a column it distributes HEIGHT; width already fills because the renderer only sets `align-items` when `counterAxisAlignItems` is given, so the flex default of `stretch` applies. FILL is correct only for children of a HORIZONTAL frame, which is why the two body columns carry it and nothing below them does. Plugin #298.",
    "Every value is the captured Dataset's (COUNT BY ORDER STATUS, manufacturing.zeenea.app, 2026-09-30). The three sections are shared parts; this page gives them its values through each SECTION node's `values`.",
    "The full description is the product's rich text: a heading, a paragraph, a schema table (drawn with `table`) and a bullet list of key characteristics, cut here after the table.",
    "The empty relations block is the product's folder illustration over \"No related Datasets\". It is drawn as the text alone: `empty-state` prints its specimen body and buttons when those props are empty (the #717 gap, still open for empty-state), and a relations block has no buttons.",
    "`tabs` has no count badge, so a count is written into the label text (\"Fields 2\").",
    "`checkbox` carries its own label here (\"Use source description\"); the product has no \"Switch to rich text\" control on this page any more."
  ],
